### I. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY & VULNERABILITY AUDIT

* **Classification**: `SV-3 (Moderate Operational Friction)`
* **Vector Identified**: Caregiver Exemption Exploitation & Cross-Watershed Rotational Free-Riding via Article 5.6.
* **Failure Mode**: Article 5.6 previously granted *ipso jure* civic rotational labor exemptions for family and community caregiving without codifying statutory dependent-to-caregiver ratios or empirical clinical impairment thresholds. Cohesive residential or kin factions were thus able to assign multiple able-bodied adults as full-time caregivers to a single dependent, immunizing the entire usufruct group from rotational infrastructure rosters. When sortition panels reviewed contested exemptions, the absence of documentary thresholds forced juries into asymmetric moral loss aversion, resulting in high false-negative exemption approvals. This created labor deficits that were systematically externalized onto adjacent watershed cohorts under Article 10.3 mutual aid protocols, generating civic resentment and localized assembly deadlocks.
* **Resolution**: The vulnerability is closed by establishing precise, non-invasive biophysical dependency ratios (capping exemptions at a 1:1 adult-to-dependent baseline absent documented multi-person somatic requirements), binding sortition panel reviews to objective functional independence ledgers, and formalizing automatic administrative re-queueing without violating Chapter I Invariants (no carceral sanction, no eviction, no deprivation of Class-A survival baselines).

